  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget and round cap are both exhausted (400/400 evals, round 4 of 4), and the front is feasible and well-covered, so no further exploration is possible or useful. Feasibility is established: 315/400 evaluations meet both constraints (0% throughput violations, best 201 MSPS vs the 1 MSPS floor; 21% error violations, best 5.53e-08 = 2^-24.11 vs the 2^-10 limit). The Pareto front spans area_um2 6860..15159 against the HV reference 40000 and accuracy_bits 10.1..24.1 against the HV reference 10, i.e. it covers essentially the full useful accuracy range and a wide area range, and all four registry families have been explored (none remaining). The spec's selection rule (min area_um2) is already satisfied by the front's low-area corner: iterative [data_width=15 n_iter=12 angle_guard=1 frac_guard=0 rounding=round] at area_um2=6860, accuracy_bits=10.1 (max_abs_err=0.000917 <= 0.000976562), throughput 9.43 MSPS >= 1 MSPS — a design that meets both constraints with margin on throughput and error. Improvement has saturated: hypervolume gain this round was only +0.4%, and the pipelined/pipelined_m families (the only high-throughput options) produced 0 feasible designs in 20 combined evaluations, so they cannot improve the constrained front. No constraint is unreachable, so `infeasible` is not warranted.",
  "next_plan": null
}
